<title>JAPAN: Japan April aluminium mill output, shipments up.</title>
<headline>Japan April aluminium mill output, shipments up.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese shipments of fabricated aluminium products rose 8.1 percent to a record 225,303 tonnes in April from the same period last year, the Japan Aluminum Federation said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The April data was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   April 97	yr/yr change  March 97 (revised)</p>
<p> Output	   226,224	+6.9 pct	 228,699 (+7.6 pct)</p>
<p>   Flat-rolled  116,826	+6.2 pct	 117,727 (+5.3)</p>
<p>   Extrusions   109,418	+7.6 pct	 110,972 (+10.2)</p>
<p> Shipments	225,303	+8.1 pct	 224,983 (+7.9)</p>
<p>   Flat-rolled  116,269	+7.9 pct	 113,955 (+4.4)</p>
<p>   Extrusions   109,034	+8.4 pct	 111,028 (+11.7)</p>
<p> Inventories     87,763	+4.0 pct	  86,349 (+6.4)</p>
<p>   Flat-rolled   73,091	+5.7 pct	  72,344</p>
<p>   Extrusions    14,672	-3.7 pct	  14,005</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
